What follows are spoilers for version 3.1.1.  If you're still playing 3.0j,
none of the stuff regarding quests applies, as 3.0j doesn't have quests.

In article <dennisb.735595193@sfu.ca> dennisb@kits.sfu.ca (Mercury Fox) writes:

>...I still don't know HOW you go on a quest, of HOW you get to the Fort, or
>HOW you get to the Tower Of Balance!!!  So how do you do these things?  And
>how would a person who has no access to rec.games.hack learn these types of
>things???

Going on a quest:  Once you reach a certain level of the dungeon (I think it's
	between 11th & 15th) your mentor will send you a telepathic message
	requesting you to go on a quest.  Somewhere on that level will be a
	magic portal that will take you to him.  You have to be 14th level
	before you will be permitted to go on the quest.  Don't concern
	yourself too much until both of those things happen.

Fort Ludios:  One of the Magic Memory Vaults in the dungeon occasionally has a
	magic portal in it that will transport you to Fort Ludios, Croesus'
	castle.  It contains literally hundreds of soldiers, a throne room,
	and a room filled with gold.

	The Tower of Balance is merely the place to which Wizard characters
are summoned to learn of their quest.

	The quest is explained rather throughly in the context of the game,
while Fort Ludios really is not necessary to complete the game.  Perhaps the
developers intended it as something of an 'easter egg.'

>One more thing, in the Medusa level, is there anything that you are suppose to
